= Descriptive Statistics

There is an underlying population from which a repressentative sample with $n$ observations, it is represented by a vector

$ y = (y_1, y_2, dots, y_n) $

Then sorted

$
  y = (y_(( 1 )), y_(( 2 )), dots, y_((n)) )
$

Where $y_((1))$ is the smallest observed sample and $y_((n))$ is the largest.

